    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57">

                <pb facs="0070" n="58" xml:id="pg58"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8890/9735/6: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-31T22:00:00+04:00">October 31,
                            1942—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 2—2:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>98. British Minister<anchor n="17" xml:id="d57-f1"/> and I have right along been
                    in entire agreement re subject of your 52, October 27. He feels as you and I
                    that if we can accommodate Afghan Government in small matters we should do so.
                    We need, of course, make no promises re 1942 lamb skin crop … Incidentally
                    British Minister states India does not want Afghan wool.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d57-f1" n="17" xml:id="d57-f1-content">
